{{- /* The git signing public key as a bare `ssh-ed25519 AAAA…` string, from
       Proton Pass, falling back to the agent. Renders empty if neither answers,
       and config.tmpl then omits user.signingkey so commits fail loudly.

       Every call here must stay guarded, because chezmoi's `output` aborts the
       whole template — and with it the whole apply — on a non-zero exit. The
       `|| true` in the sh wrapper is what keeps a bad day from taking the
       apply down with it.

       This used to call chezmoi's `protonPass`, which offers no such escape:
       it aborts on any pass-cli failure. Guarding it on "a session exists" was
       not enough, because a live session says nothing about *this item* — a
       renamed item, a renamed field, a lapsed share or a transient 422 each
       still aborted the entire apply over a git config file that has a
       perfectly good fallback sitting in the agent. An unreadable signing key
       should cost the signing key, nothing more.

       The pass:// URI stays the single literal the vault reference is written
       as, and the vault, title and field are split out of it rather than
       restated: dotfiles-secrets-check derives both what to read and what to
       render by scanning the tree for exactly that shape, so spelling them out
       as pass-cli flags instead would quietly drop this file out of the health
       check.

       Arguments reach sh positionally rather than interpolated into the
       command string, so a title containing a quote character cannot break out
       of it.

       Addressed by vault name and item title, not by share/item id. A PAT
       session's vault access is a share, so re-authenticating mints a new
       share id and any id pinned here goes stale — which fails as a 422.
       Titles survive that, and are how the restore script and secrets-check
       already name items.

       No is-container or has-proton-session guard: pass-cli missing, no
       session and an unreadable item all arrive here as empty output and take
       the agent fallback, which is the right answer in a container
       anyway. */ -}}
{{- $uri := printf "pass://%s/git signing key/public_key" (includeTemplate "vault-name" .) -}}
{{- $p := splitList "/" (trimPrefix "pass://" $uri) -}}
{{- $key := output "sh" "-c" `pass-cli item view --vault-name "$1" --item-title "$2" --field "$3" 2>/dev/null || true` "sh" (index $p 0) (index $p 1) (index $p 2) | trim -}}
{{- if $key -}}
{{- $key -}}
{{- else -}}
{{- output "sh" "-c" "ssh-add -L 2>/dev/null | awk '/git-signing/{print $1\" \"$2; exit}'" | trim -}}
{{- end -}}
